{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"One Root","html":"<article id='sn1.44'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.44 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 1.44 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>5. Ādittavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>5. On Fire </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ekamūlasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One Root </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ekamūlaṁ dvirāvaṭṭaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“One the root, two the loops, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>timalaṁ pañcapattharaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>three the stains, five the spreads, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Samuddaṁ dvādasāvaṭṭaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and the ocean, the twelfth whirlpool: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pātālaṁ atarī isī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>such is the abyss crossed by the seer.” </span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
